// spec: under --no-implicit-fallthrough (design.md "No implicit fallthrough", rules 2, 3, 5 and 6) a case's last `break;` (also ending a block that ends the case) is an error naming its removal, `[[fallthrough]];` one naming `fallthrough;` (F's form, design.md 23e), `fallthrough;` inside another statement, in the last case or outside a switch an error, and so is a label nested in another statement (Duff's device); a case whose end is reached is no error any more (step 1's "runs on into it"): it breaks; nor is an empty case (`case 7:` beside `case 8:`), each label beginning a group of its own that does nothing when empty, or a group of `fallthrough;` alone, which shares the next group's body (kovarex, 2026-11-08)
// kpp: --no-implicit-fallthrough --no-std
// error: no_implicit_fallthrough_errors_is_error.kpp:20: error: every case ends with a break: remove `break;` (design.md "No implicit fallthrough")
// error: no_implicit_fallthrough_errors_is_error.kpp:24: error: every case ends with a break: remove `break;` (design.md "No implicit fallthrough")
// error: no_implicit_fallthrough_errors_is_error.kpp:27: error: a case runs on into the next by `fallthrough;` alone: write `fallthrough;`, not `[[fallthrough]];` (design.md "No implicit fallthrough")
// error: no_implicit_fallthrough_errors_is_error.kpp:30: error: fallthrough; is the last statement of a case with another case after it, which it runs on into: not inside another statement, in the last case or outside a switch (design.md "No implicit fallthrough")
// error: no_implicit_fallthrough_errors_is_error.kpp:37: error: a case label is a statement of its switch's body: nested in another statement it means nothing where every case ends with a break (design.md "No implicit fallthrough")
// error: no_implicit_fallthrough_errors_is_error.kpp:42: error: fallthrough; is the last statement of a case with another case after it, which it runs on into: not inside another statement, in the last case or outside a switch (design.md "No implicit fallthrough")
// error: no_implicit_fallthrough_errors_is_error.kpp:44: error: fallthrough; is the last statement of a case with another case after it, which it runs on into: not inside another statement, in the last case or outside a switch (design.md "No implicit fallthrough")
// no-warning: runs on into it
// no-warning: no_implicit_fallthrough_errors_is_error.kpp:52:
// no-warning: no_implicit_fallthrough_errors_is_error.kpp:56:
int f(int x)
{
  int r = 0;
  switch (x)
  {
    case 0:
      r = 1;
      break;
    case 1:
    {
      r = 2;
      break;
    }
    case 2:
      [[fallthrough]];
    case 3:
      if (r == 0)
        fallthrough;
      r = 3;
    case 4:
      r = 4;
    case 5:
      while (r < 10)
      {
        case 6:
          ++r;
      }
    default:
      r = 9;
      fallthrough;
  }
  fallthrough;
  return r;
}
int g(int x)
{
  int r = 0;
  switch (x)
  {
    case 7:
    case 8:
      r = 8;
    case 9:
      fallthrough;
    case 10:
      r = 10;
  }
  return r;
}
int main()
{
  return f(0) + g(7);
}
